# team-programming A/B — server-side associative reduce pushdown
#
# Same command, same script, same machine, one player at a time under the shared
# lock. The baseline image predates bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py, so the
# script is bind-mounted into both runs; the driver API it calls is unchanged.
#
# command (baseline):
#   flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline -v "$PWD/bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py:/src/bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py:ro" fpq-baseline python3 /src/bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py'
# command (change):
#   flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=programming -v "$PWD/bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py:/src/bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py:ro" fpq-programming python3 /src/bench/jobs/aggregate-pushdown.py'
#
# What it runs: Cursor.aggregate("SELECT price FROM fp_agg_bench",
# {"price_sum": ("sum", "price"), "rows": ("count_all", None)}, size=batch) over
# 2,000,000 rows, checked against the server's SELECT sum(price), count(*).
# "B shipped" is the sum of the data segment's published payload_size over the
# frames the reduce actually consumed; "max" is the largest single frame. Time is
# the median of 5 timed calls after a warm one, and excludes the untimed byte
# measurement. The change's frame count includes the terminal empty scalar frame
# (56 B) that closes the stream; the baseline writes its terminal empty NEXT but
# the loop breaks before reading it.
#
# --- baseline: main@7e3d2e6, client-side reduce (FPCOLUMN batch + C++ walk) ---
### ENV
cpu: AMD Ryzen 7 7700 8-Core Processor
mem: 30 GiB
ghz: 3.8
cores: 8
postgres: 18.6
python: 3.13.5
sqlalchemy: 2.0.40
pyarrow: 26.0.0
adbc: 1.13.0
shape: bench
git: baseline
shm: 3.0G
### END ENV

AGGREGATE (sum(int8) + count_all): 2000000 rows through Cursor.aggregate
    2000000    100000    206.73 ms     9.67M rows/s    16251040 B shipped in 20  frames (max   812552 B)  ±2.8%  ok
    2000000   2000000    162.91 ms    12.28M rows/s    16250056 B shipped in 1   frames (max 16250056 B)  ±1.9%  ok
  result: price_sum=999000000 rows=2000000 (server 999000000, 2000000)

# --- change: team/programming, worker-side reduce (FPREDUCE scalar frame) ---
