AGGREGATE (sum(int8) + count_all): 2000000 rows through Cursor.aggregate
    2000000    100000    184.03 ms    10.87M rows/s        1176 B shipped in 21  frames (max       56 B)  ±3.0%  ok
    2000000   2000000    155.59 ms    12.85M rows/s         112 B shipped in 2   frames (max       56 B)  ±5.0%  ok
  result: price_sum=999000000 rows=2000000 (server 999000000, 2000000)

### AB
# batch=100000 (driver default): 206.73 -> 184.03 ms (-11.0%, 1.123x faster;
# 9.67 -> 10.87M rows/s, +12.4%); bytes shipped 16,251,040 -> 1,176 B (-99.9928%,
# 13,818x less; the 20 data frames alone are 16,251,040 -> 1,120 B, 14,510x less;
# max frame 812,552 -> 56 B). Same 2,000,000 rows, same scalar result, ok.
# batch=2000000 (one request): 162.91 -> 155.59 ms (-4.5%, 1.047x faster;
# 12.28 -> 12.85M rows/s, +4.6%); bytes 16,250,056 -> 112 B (-99.9993%,
# 145,090x less; one data frame is 16,250,056 -> 56 B). ok.
